   "note": "drawing - the front view. From the cord end: a plate with the earth screw, one plate with two breakers, four outlet blocks of eight with the controller between the second and the third, and the far end. Outlet positions are the centres of each outlet as drawn; the outlet pitch is not dimensioned."
  },
  "input": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - 'INPUT PLUG: IEC 60309 2P+E 6H 32A/30A(24A DERATED)', 'INPUT VOLTAGE: 200-240VAC', 'INPUT PHASE: SINGLE-PHASE', 'RATED POWER: 7.4 / 5.8kVA (DUAL RATED)', 'PDU TO BE WIRED LINE TO NEUTRAL'. Sheet 2 gives the plain part number a 3 m cord. The cord is one part at the cord end; its length and the plug's face are not drawn."
  },
  "method": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "FIGURES FROM THE MAKER'S VECTOR DRAWING. Panduit customer drawing P32E06M_DC rev 06A (12/16/2022), two sheets, is a vector sheet drawn to no stated scale, with a front, rear, left, right and bottom view. Its scale was taken from its own 1750.0 overall dimension (the 1555.0 between the buttons agrees), and every position was read off renderings of the front view at 400 and 800 dpi, to about 1 mm across and 3 mm along the strip. The library draws the PDU STANDING, cord end down, so a position along the drawing becomes 1750 minus that, and a position across becomes x. No photograph and no 3D model of the part is held."
  },
  "mount": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "`rack-side`: the strip stands beside a rack's upright on two mounting buttons on its back, 1555.0 apart and 40.5 from the cord end (rear view). The drawing says 'VERTICAL, 0U, FULL' and gives no count of units; `ru: 39` is the whole units the 1750 mm length covers (39.4) and is not stated by any document."
  },
  "outlets": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - '(24) C13, (8) C19', numbered 1 to 32 across the four blocks as the front view prints them (the numerals are read from the drawing and not every one is legible at its size); each block is a C19, three C13, three C13 and a C19, the C13s staggered across the face. Each outlet is std/c13-outlet@1 or std/c19-outlet@1. The way up of each outlet is read off the front view."
  },
  "rear": {
